🚀 Purpose of an MVP
Validate demand: Test if customers truly want your solution.

Reduce risk: Avoid wasting time and money on features nobody needs.

Gather feedback: Learn how users interact and what improvements matter most.

Enable iteration: Use the build–measure–learn cycle to refine or pivot.
