📊 MVP vs. Other Concepts
Term	What it is	Key Difference
Prototype	Rough, often non-functional model	Tests feasibility/design, not real users
Demo	Presentation layer for stakeholders	Looks good but not usable in real life
MVP	Smallest usable product	Real users can use it; generates data
MMP (Minimum Marketable Product)	First version ready for broad sales	Focused on revenue, not just learning	
