⚠️ Common Misunderstandings
❌ Not a half-finished product → An MVP must be usable, not broken.

❌ Not just a “cheap app” → It’s about validated learning, not cutting corners.

❌ Not the final product → It’s a starting point to evolve based on feedback.

✅ Key Takeaway
If you’re building something new, focus on the smallest version that solves one real problem for users and lets you measure their response. That’s your MVP.

